  "lineage": "Ayarachi is a Quechua panpipe-and-drum music and dance of Puno, kept in its older form chiefly in Paratía in Lampa province and in Cuyocuyo in Sandia, played by large troupes of men who sound big panpipes in interlocking paired halves with drums. Its slow, solemn tunes are linked in local tradition to mourning and the dead. The siku card stands in for the ayarachi panpipes and the membrane-drum card for the drums.",
